(3111412, 437813, 27767, '<td valign="top">Cute shot for sure. I would be interested to see a very unique perspective in this shot, one I would not normally see otherwise (possibly from 3 or 4 inches off the ground?). Good catchlights in the eyes. I keep thinking about the off-center composition here, and my main thought is it feels unbalanced. Maybe if the tail was laying (or swinging) to the left side of the frame, or the dog was looking a little left, through the shot, it would help provide counter balance to the placement along the right 2/3rds vertical line.</td>', 'Cute shot for sure. I would be interested to see a very unique perspective in this shot, one I would not normally see otherwise (possibly from 3 or 4 inches off the ground?). Good catchlights in the eyes. I keep thinking about the off-center composition here, and my main thought is it feels unbalanced. Maybe if the tail was laying (or swinging) to the left side of the frame, or the dog was looking a little left, through the shot, it would help provide counter balance to the placement along the right 2/3rds vertical line.', '2006-12-13 01:51:27.000000', NULL, 1),
