(3121342, 435779, 68504, '<td valign="top">Great light and colour.  (Pissed off but forbearing cat?)</td>', 'Great light and colour.  (Pissed off but forbearing cat?)', '2006-12-15 15:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121344, 437902, 208, '<td valign="top">This is a technically bad picture (though it sure is in focus), but you''ve captured a hilarious moment that makes up for it.</td>', 'This is a technically bad picture (though it sure is in focus), but you''ve captured a hilarious moment that makes up for it.', '2006-12-15 15:53:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121346, 436847, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Nice portrait, toning works well and makes this quite unique.  Just wish the eyes were as sharp as the ears/nose seem to be.  Perhaps a fraction more contrast may have given this more depth.  Like the composition, just looks like it needs a slight rotate.. up left.</td>', '6 - Nice portrait, toning works well and makes this quite unique.  Just wish the eyes were as sharp as the ears/nose seem to be.  Perhaps a fraction more contrast may have given this more depth.  Like the composition, just looks like it needs a slight rotate.. up left.', '2006-12-15 15:54:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121356, 436034, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice image of the horse.  Your call (obviously), but think just a little less empty space on left for more balance make this even better in my opinion.  For this Challenge, with this image, I also think including the name of the horse, would have given this more character and made it more ''personal''.</td>', '7 - Nice image of the horse.  Your call (obviously), but think just a little less empty space on left for more balance make this even better in my opinion.  For this Challenge, with this image, I also think including the name of the horse, would have given this more character and made it more ''personal''.', '2006-12-15 15:57:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121359, 436363, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Different.  Focus seems sharpest on the backdrop, which is also too dominant in my opinion.  More refined crop on the left too where the dog''s paw is coming into frame.</td>', '6 - Different.  Focus seems sharpest on the backdrop, which is also too dominant in my opinion.  More refined crop on the left too where the dog''s paw is coming into frame.', '2006-12-15 15:59:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121366, 438064, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Very nice, toning works well.  Nice composition/crop.  Just a little more clarity/pop on the eye and there is an odd ''edge''/something just above Ginger''s nose ridge.</td>', '8 - Very nice, toning works well.  Nice composition/crop.  Just a little more clarity/pop on the eye and there is an odd ''edge''/something just above Ginger''s nose ridge.', '2006-12-15 16:00:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121368, 436695, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Sharper/more clarity on the eyes (even with the soft effect) and the right side not so cropped/chopped, make this even better in my opinion.</td>', '6 - Sharper/more clarity on the eyes (even with the soft effect) and the right side not so cropped/chopped, make this even better in my opinion.', '2006-12-15 16:01:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121370, 435355, 208, '<td valign="top">Well, nice job on the lighting and focus and etc. And 1,000 bonus points for being able to keep three dogs and a cat still long enough to get the shot. But ... I''m just not a fan of this kind of studio portrait. They''re all just sort of sitting there. I''m not getting any read on any of their personalities, and the lack of a background doesn''t really help. I also get the feeling I''ll be one of the few who think that way. Sorry.</td>', 'Well, nice job on the lighting and focus and etc. And 1,000 bonus points for being able to keep three dogs and a cat still long enough to get the shot. But ... I''m just not a fan of this kind of studio portrait. They''re all just sort of sitting there. I''m not getting any read on any of their personalities, and the lack of a background doesn''t really help. I also get the feeling I''ll be one of the few who think that way. Sorry.', '2006-12-15 16:02:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121371, 437991, 63779, '<td valign="top">I really like this portrait. The dog looks very at home in the environment. Unfortunately the blurry bush (cactus maybe?) in the lower left is very distracting--I cannot keep my eye from it.</td>', 'I really like this portrait. The dog looks very at home in the environment. Unfortunately the blurry bush (cactus maybe?) in the lower left is very distracting--I cannot keep my eye from it.', '2006-12-15 16:02:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121377, 435968, 208, '<td valign="top">OK - this is stupid and doesn''t take away from the overall quality of the shot, but ... could you get rid of that yellow speck in the bottom left? Just continue the blue square. kthxbye!</td>', 'OK - this is stupid and doesn''t take away from the overall quality of the shot, but ... could you get rid of that yellow speck in the bottom left? Just continue the blue square. kthxbye!', '2006-12-15 16:04:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121379, 438020, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - Nice big pupil capture on Misty.  Don''t mind the b&amp;w but not sure the pp has made it work as well for the image as some more tweaking may have done.  Seems to be a bit of grain/noise.  The crop at the ears more finely tuned and this larger (if quality was there), make this better in my opinion.</td>', '3 - Nice big pupil capture on Misty.  Don''t mind the b&w but not sure the pp has made it work as well for the image as some more tweaking may have done.  Seems to be a bit of grain/noise.  The crop at the ears more finely tuned and this larger (if quality was there), make this better in my opinion.', '2006-12-15 16:05:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121384, 436956, 39850, '<td valign="top">4 - Looks like difficult fur to capture using artificial light.  Base/background colors, whilst do ''fit in'' with the dog''s coloring, perhaps placing the dog on a different color may have brought out the nice ''silver tones'' in the fur more.  Variation in angle/perspective likely have helped give this less of a ''snapshottish'' type feel, in my opinion.</td>', '4 - Looks like difficult fur to capture using artificial light.  Base/background colors, whilst do ''fit in'' with the dog''s coloring, perhaps placing the dog on a different color may have brought out the nice ''silver tones'' in the fur more.  Variation in angle/perspective likely have helped give this less of a ''snapshottish'' type feel, in my opinion.', '2006-12-15 16:07:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121386, 437641, 208, '<td valign="top">I''d tighten the crop closer to the pooch and hydrant. I think it''s safe for the hydrant''s shadow to run out of the frame sooner if you keep the dog''s.</td>', 'I''d tighten the crop closer to the pooch and hydrant. I think it''s safe for the hydrant''s shadow to run out of the frame sooner if you keep the dog''s.', '2006-12-15 16:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121391, 437951, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Different.  A bit too much pp/effects/something going on here in my opinion, especially for a fairly cursory look at while voting.  Likely looks as you intended though, so your call, obviously.</td>', '6 - Different.  A bit too much pp/effects/something going on here in my opinion, especially for a fairly cursory look at while voting.  Likely looks as you intended though, so your call, obviously.', '2006-12-15 16:08:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3121392, 438111, 68504, '<td valign="top">Like the pose and mood and bw a lot.  (Would a lesser exposure to get rid of blown highlights have prejudiced the subtle exposure of head?) P.S. Comment does not reflect how much I liked this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-20 02:57:30.</i></td>', 'Like the pose and mood and bw a lot.  (Would a lesser exposure to get rid of blown highlights have prejudiced the subtle exposure of head?) P.S. Comment does not reflect how much I liked this.', '2006-12-15 16:08:54.000000', '2006-12-20 02:57:30.000000', 1),
