(3130564, 437803, 39850, '<td valign="top">5 - Nice concept and composition.  Just wish ''red'' was ''bigger'' within the frame and more light on him/her.  Perhaps also a cropping out of the hill/something rear left, but fairly minor.</td>', '5 - Nice concept and composition.  Just wish ''red'' was ''bigger'' within the frame and more light on him/her.  Perhaps also a cropping out of the hill/something rear left, but fairly minor.', '2006-12-19 04:57:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130565, 438101, 52130, '<td valign="top">bryantbus????? I can''t tell, it looks just like the "ivory cat" except a flipped imaged and you gave that kitty a serious haircut. I mean...how many duo-toned eyed kitties are there out there? Nice shot anyways, although the edges of the fur look almost shaved off in a weird way. It''s probably just the white on white that''s throwing me off though.</td>', 'bryantbus????? I can''t tell, it looks just like the "ivory cat" except a flipped imaged and you gave that kitty a serious haircut. I mean...how many duo-toned eyed kitties are there out there? Nice shot anyways, although the edges of the fur look almost shaved off in a weird way. It''s probably just the white on white that''s throwing me off though.', '2006-12-19 04:57:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130569, 437374, 39850, '<td valign="top">4 - Like the concept including the straight on and the decorative ''lines'' in the background.  Biggest detractor for me in this image is the ''haze'' so more clarity and ''pop'' as well as 640 make this better in my opinion.</td>', '4 - Like the concept including the straight on and the decorative ''lines'' in the background.  Biggest detractor for me in this image is the ''haze'' so more clarity and ''pop'' as well as 640 make this better in my opinion.', '2006-12-19 04:58:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130573, 436700, 39850, '<td valign="top">4 - Whilst the framing does work in my opinion, at this size, it is sacrificing too much screen space for this particular Challenge.  Perhaps the fabric a little more subtle andthe eyes open more and that white paw included make this even better.</td>', '4 - Whilst the framing does work in my opinion, at this size, it is sacrificing too much screen space for this particular Challenge.  Perhaps the fabric a little more subtle andthe eyes open more and that white paw included make this even better.', '2006-12-19 04:59:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130579, 437065, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Really like the set up and concept and lighting, but something is holding this back from being a stand out image.. not sure exactly what.  Perhaps the framing, also the fabric a bit more subtle and the folds/etc selectively ''placed'' and perhaps a more horizontal or square framing, not sure.  There is some visible grain in the black fabric, so, as well as perhaps enhancing the dog, a selective softening/something may have helped to minimize that.  Also, 640 would have helped.</td>', '6 - Really like the set up and concept and lighting, but something is holding this back from being a stand out image.. not sure exactly what.  Perhaps the framing, also the fabric a bit more subtle and the folds/etc selectively ''placed'' and perhaps a more horizontal or square framing, not sure.  There is some visible grain in the black fabric, so, as well as perhaps enhancing the dog, a selective softening/something may have helped to minimize that.  Also, 640 would have helped.', '2006-12-19 05:02:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130581, 437833, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Nice clean shot, wish it was not so tightly cropped and so horizontally framed, perhaps more fabric included for balance, may have made this even better in my opinion.  The movement in the ear, but minor.</td>', '6 - Nice clean shot, wish it was not so tightly cropped and so horizontally framed, perhaps more fabric included for balance, may have made this even better in my opinion.  The movement in the ear, but minor.', '2006-12-19 05:04:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130583, 436983, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - This is good, but wish it was 640.  Undecided on the ''off'' diagonal lines/patterns, but do like the dof and the use of it.  Wish it was not so chopped on the right, and perhaps a little less space on the left. <i>edit:typo</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-20 05:47:26.</i></td>', '6 - This is good, but wish it was 640.  Undecided on the ''off'' diagonal lines/patterns, but do like the dof and the use of it.  Wish it was not so chopped on the right, and perhaps a little less space on the left. edit:typo', '2006-12-19 05:05:09.000000', '2006-12-20 05:47:26.000000', 1),
(3130584, 437641, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - It is, but for a Pet Portrait Challenge, I think this would have been much better if the dog was dominating the image more.</td>', '2 - It is, but for a Pet Portrait Challenge, I think this would have been much better if the dog was dominating the image more.', '2006-12-19 05:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130588, 436354, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - Good potential.  Less kid (pun intended) and more goat and bigger, make this much better for this Challenge in my opinion.</td>', '2 - Good potential.  Less kid (pun intended) and more goat and bigger, make this much better for this Challenge in my opinion.', '2006-12-19 05:07:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130592, 436960, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - A little blurry and flash/lighting issues.  Background not enhancing ''Peper''.  Best focus seems to be on the nose and in the mouth, so.. adjusting that to be best on the eyes would have helped this in my opinion.  Looks ''snapshottish''.</td>', '3 - A little blurry and flash/lighting issues.  Background not enhancing ''Peper''.  Best focus seems to be on the nose and in the mouth, so.. adjusting that to be best on the eyes would have helped this in my opinion.  Looks ''snapshottish''.', '2006-12-19 05:08:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130594, 436503, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice clarity.  Works as is, but do wonder about the ear not chopped.  Perhaps a more refined crop on the left too, where the darker fur comes in.</td>', '7 - Nice clarity.  Works as is, but do wonder about the ear not chopped.  Perhaps a more refined crop on the left too, where the darker fur comes in.', '2006-12-19 05:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130597, 437225, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Nice concept.  Difficult to get this visually balanced, perhaps offsetting it more and a tighter crop on the left, may have given this an edge.  Also like to have seen the ''real cat'' sharper, more ''pop''.  Not sure on the heavy frame, including color choice, but your call, obviously.</td>', '6 - Nice concept.  Difficult to get this visually balanced, perhaps offsetting it more and a tighter crop on the left, may have given this an edge.  Also like to have seen the ''real cat'' sharper, more ''pop''.  Not sure on the heavy frame, including color choice, but your call, obviously.', '2006-12-19 05:10:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130600, 438054, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice capture, including of a ''dog''s life''.  Difficult, but even sharper on the eyes, make this better in my opinion.  Minor, but the blue something between the dog''s head and forearm detracts slightly, but obviously opportune.</td>', '7 - Nice capture, including of a ''dog''s life''.  Difficult, but even sharper on the eyes, make this better in my opinion.  Minor, but the blue something between the dog''s head and forearm detracts slightly, but obviously opportune.', '2006-12-19 05:12:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130605, 435443, 39850, '<td valign="top">9 - Very nice.  Very nice scene and colors.  Just wonder about with the space either side of the cat whether a fraction more above the head would have visually balanced this out even better, but then the cat would be smaller, so who knows.  Otherwise, maybe just a little tighter either side.  Again, white framing works well, but at this size, I''d just like to have seen the cat bigger.  Difficult, but more detail discernible in the cat too.</td>', '9 - Very nice.  Very nice scene and colors.  Just wonder about with the space either side of the cat whether a fraction more above the head would have visually balanced this out even better, but then the cat would be smaller, so who knows.  Otherwise, maybe just a little tighter either side.  Again, white framing works well, but at this size, I''d just like to have seen the cat bigger.  Difficult, but more detail discernible in the cat too.', '2006-12-19 05:14:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3130608, 437844, 39850, '<td valign="top">3 - For a Pet Portrait, whilst not a bad action/character shot, the blur/issues dominate too much in my opinion and I''d rather have seen a ''still'' shot.</td>', '3 - For a Pet Portrait, whilst not a bad action/character shot, the blur/issues dominate too much in my opinion and I''d rather have seen a ''still'' shot.', '2006-12-19 05:16:35.000000', NULL, 1),
