(3157605, 436035, 31606, '<td valign="top">Very nice portrait.  I think a tigher crop might work .  Maybe just cropping out the post on the right of the image.  You have nice tones in the B/W and nice sharpness.  Also a very nice bokeh effect with the background to eliminate distraction.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-28 22:19:51.</i></td>', 'Very nice portrait.  I think a tigher crop might work .  Maybe just cropping out the post on the right of the image.  You have nice tones in the B/W and nice sharpness.  Also a very nice bokeh effect with the background to eliminate distraction.', '2006-12-28 22:17:09.000000', '2006-12-28 22:19:51.000000', 0),
(3157649, 436797, 31606, '<td valign="top">Wel this one caught my eye.  Very nice crisp image.  That border is a little tacky which is what probably hurt you more than anything.  I don;t agree with the comment stating you need more space.  I think the crop/comp. is fine how it is.</td>', 'Wel this one caught my eye.  Very nice crisp image.  That border is a little tacky which is what probably hurt you more than anything.  I don;t agree with the comment stating you need more space.  I think the crop/comp. is fine how it is.', '2006-12-28 22:32:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157860, 437745, 50641, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully emotive shot.  I like donkeys!  You''ve gotten some good tips worth trying.  Since you can''t really do anything about the focus at this point, you could try a spitshine of one or more photoshop art filters - like poster edges, cutout, chalk and charcoal, etc.  While it wouldn''t make this crowd love it, you might still squeeze a moody, artsy image out of it.  I hope you will take more donkey pictures!</td>', 'Wonderfully emotive shot.  I like donkeys!  You''ve gotten some good tips worth trying.  Since you can''t really do anything about the focus at this point, you could try a spitshine of one or more photoshop art filters - like poster edges, cutout, chalk and charcoal, etc.  While it wouldn''t make this crowd love it, you might still squeeze a moody, artsy image out of it.  I hope you will take more donkey pictures!', '2006-12-28 23:38:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157869, 437976, 50641, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6 - really like the extreme close up and the great focus on the eye.  And I like how the green in the background matches!  You did a terrific job cloning out the eye boogie - I wish I could do that for my cat routinely, in 3D.  There is no end to his goop.</td>', 'I gave this a 6 - really like the extreme close up and the great focus on the eye.  And I like how the green in the background matches!  You did a terrific job cloning out the eye boogie - I wish I could do that for my cat routinely, in 3D.  There is no end to his goop.', '2006-12-28 23:42:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158245, 437698, 50695, '<td valign="top">This is a very good photo, insanely underrated. I gave it an 8.</td>', 'This is a very good photo, insanely underrated. I gave it an 8.', '2006-12-29 01:24:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158349, 436864, 50641, '<td valign="top">How did you get the kitties to be so interested in the flower? Great dapply background and the crop of the flower. I love the one of Rita chomping, but you chose well - Ruth has such a classic look.  I wasn''t totally sure about the title during the challenge - but now I guess it''s about eating :)</td>', 'How did you get the kitties to be so interested in the flower? Great dapply background and the crop of the flower. I love the one of Rita chomping, but you chose well - Ruth has such a classic look.  I wasn''t totally sure about the title during the challenge - but now I guess it''s about eating :)', '2006-12-29 01:48:03.000000', NULL, 0),
